<p>Slight metacritique:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4376 is to be contained</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is valid, in my opinion. Many containment procedures choose to outline the <em>desired</em> containment over the <em>current</em> containment, and that's something I honestly agree with; it saves having to update the article every time their containment situation changes. The use of &quot;to be&quot; doesn't imply that it's not currently contained, just that these procedures should be adhered to in the future <em>as well as</em> the present.</p>

